      "severity": "OBSERVATION",
      "area": "benchmarks/ViciOne.ServiceBus.Benchmark/Analytics.cs",
      "statement": "The sample == maximum branch in Histogram is redundant because Math.Clamp already maps the computed index segmentCount to segmentCount - 1. Removing the branch keeps the whole suite green, so no test holds that branch on its own.",
      "assuranceStillHeld": true,
      "reason": "The conserved histogram sum is carried by Math.Clamp plus the Count > 0 filter, both of which are held by discriminating tests."
    },
    {
      "id": "F-0054-2",
      "severity": "CORRECTED_BY_TEAM_1",
      "area": "artifacts/BenchmarkDotNet/results",
      "statement": "Three generated SerializationBenchmark reports were tracked in the repository. They entered with team 1 commit db0481d8, not with any lead commit. The benchmark console writes to artifacts/BenchmarkDotNet, which the existing ignore rule **/BenchmarkDotNet.Artifacts/**/* does not match, so every benchmark run rewrote tracked files and left the working tree dirty.",
      "correction": "11e73956",
      "verified": "A full dry job now leaves git status empty."
    },
    {
      "id": "F-0054-3",
      "severity": "OBSERVATION",
      "area": "benchmarks/ViciOne.ServiceBus.Benchmark/Latency/MessageMetricCapture.cs",
      "statement": "In the postSend path, PostSend can reach a message id before Sent recorded it. The add branch then constructs SentMessage with SendTimestamp 0, so that message would be measured from benchmark start rather than from its own send. The InMemory paths do not use postSend, so no executed run is affected.",
      "affectsExecutedRuns": false,
      "relatesTo": "the still open external transport block in benchmarks/ToDo.md"
    }
  ],
